WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.129 --> 00:00:03.969
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and this week
Guardians of the Galaxy is out in theaters

00:00:03.969 --> 00:00:07.910
so this is going to be my review. Since a
lot of you probably haven’t seen it yet

00:00:07.910 --> 00:00:12.639
I’ll do my non spoilery part first and then
when we get into spoilers I’ll talk about

00:00:12.639 --> 00:00:17.019
really specific stuff. I know they’ve already
confirmed a sequel but since I’m planning

00:00:17.019 --> 00:00:22.079
a longer video for that I’ll just briefly
mention a few possible storylines they could

00:00:22.079 --> 00:00:23.089
do from the comics.

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:26.630
Hello any new people, if you’re just finding
me for the first time I do Marvel videos every

00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:28.569
week. Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:00:28.569 --> 00:00:35.250
Most of you probably at least know who the
Guardians are even if you’ve never read

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:41.610
the comics. The biggest generalization is
Space Avengers. A bunch of super assholes

00:00:41.610 --> 00:00:45.460
come together to form a team and keep the
villains from destroying the galaxy. Which

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:49.320
galaxy you ask? Generally it’s assumed in
this movie that it’s the Milky Way galaxy

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:51.590
but they never say officially.

00:00:51.590 --> 00:00:54.450
Most of what you’ve probably been hearing
about the movie is how much everyone loves

00:00:54.450 --> 00:01:00.060
it, which is surprising. But a lot of the
credit for that goes to director James Gunn.

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:04.589
He directed and wrote the script. He’s mostly
known for really small cult films like Slither

00:01:04.589 --> 00:01:09.810
with Nathan Fillion, who did have a funny
cameo in Guardians. Gunn has this really amazing

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:13.490
visual and literary sense.

00:01:13.490 --> 00:01:17.590
The executives at Marvel Studios have a lot
of say over what stuff looks like and sounds

00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:21.319
like in the end, but Guardians has this really
steam punky classic Star Wars feel with 80s

00:01:21.319 --> 00:01:25.060
pop culture jokes throughout. And James Gunn
is the reason for that.

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:30.490
The other really important thing that you
can thank Gunn for is the bangin’ soundtrack.

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:34.920
They’ve been marketing it as the Awesome
Mix #1. Hooked on a Feeling is the song they’ve

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:37.959
been using the most in all the clips. But
there’s a laundry list of other classic

00:01:37.959 --> 00:01:39.499
70s and 80s songs.

00:01:39.499 --> 00:01:43.539
The mixtape is something that flows from Chris
Pratt’s Star Lord character, and the director

00:01:43.539 --> 00:01:50.539
has a lot of influence over how character
details get expressed. So of all the things

00:01:51.399 --> 00:01:55.069
to love about the movie, the thing you should
be most grateful for is James Gunn and the

00:01:55.069 --> 00:01:57.039
way he treated the material.

00:01:57.039 --> 00:02:00.299
Of all the actors my favorite performances
were of course Chris Pratt, who seems like

00:02:00.299 --> 00:02:04.259
he’s stepped up the most of all the other
actors. Bradley Cooper as Rocket Racoon and

00:02:04.259 --> 00:02:05.279
Vin Diesel as Groot.

00:02:05.279 --> 00:02:08.500
The reason I gave extra high fives to Chris
Pratt is because of all the other actors in

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:12.960
the film, he is the least experienced in terms
of big blockbuster movies, especially action

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:16.940
movies. And he’s the lead, he’s on screen
the most. So if he didn’t bring it, the

00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:20.640
movie would suck no matter how cool James
Gunn made it look and sound.

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:24.880
Trust me, you get the whole tone of his performance
in the first five minutes he’s on screen.

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:31.770
He has a great introduction. Bradley Cooper
and Vin Diesel have been action stars for

00:02:31.770 --> 00:02:36.240
a long time, so I judge them a lot harder.
But because they’re mo cap, they have to

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:39.890
do everything with just their voice.

00:02:39.890 --> 00:02:44.760
The visual effects artists control their expressions,
the digital character movements and reactions,

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:51.760
and those are great. But it all starts with
the voice.

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:57.610
Bradley Cooper speaks with this really fun
brogue that makes you completely forget he’s

00:02:57.610 --> 00:03:01.900
Bradley Cooper and allows you to just enjoy
this really foul mouthed cynical raccoon.

00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:06.440
And Vin Diesel only gets three words he’s
allowed to speak. Well four lines, but really

00:03:06.440 --> 00:03:07.540
it’s just three.

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:12.430
I think they said he recorded all of his takes
in five languages. So when people see the

00:03:12.430 --> 00:03:16.370
movie in Spanish or French. He won’t say
I am groot. He’ll say the translations and

00:03:16.370 --> 00:03:18.300
it’s really him doing it all. They didn’t
hire foreign language actors to come in.

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:22.540
He totally sells Groot, but a lot of the added
fun of that character is in his physical expressions

00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:23.470
and the way he reacts with his face. And yes,
they did mo-cap Vin Diesel and Bradley Cooper’s

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:24.180
faces, so when the characters smile or yell.
It’s like a billion pixels modeled on top

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:24.320
of their real life expressions.

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:31.320
Karen Gillan was so much fun to watch as a
villain. Full disclosure, if you haven’t

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:35.680
seen all my Doctor Who videos, I’ve been
a fan of hers since her ginger days as Amy

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:39.850
Pond. All I can say is the little screen time
she gets is a lot of fun. I feel like saying

00:03:39.850 --> 00:03:42.980
more about her would be spoilery. So I’ll
save some of that for later in this video.

00:03:42.980 --> 00:03:48.990
Lee Pace, for any Pushing Daisies or Thranduil
fans, is also a lot of fun to watch as a crazy

00:03:48.990 --> 00:03:53.120
insane villain. Seriously, no joke. He is
over the top batshit crazy. And I totally

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:56.990
bought it. He’s covered in makeup head to
toe, so you completely forget who’s underneath

00:03:56.990 --> 00:03:59.050
and you just focus on the voice.

00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:05.030
Benicio Del Toro is another person who’s
not on screen for a lot of time like Karen

00:04:05.030 --> 00:04:07.650
Gillan, but totally sells this ridiculous
sounding character. He plays the Collector

00:04:07.650 --> 00:04:12.340
and as small as his part is, he becomes a
huge part of the Marvel Universe. Del Toro

00:04:12.340 --> 00:04:16.500
even described himself in the movie as like
a Space Liberace. So you should definitely

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:20.870
think of his acting choices as being completely
intentional. The affectations he brings to

00:04:20.870 --> 00:04:21.600
the character.

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:27.930
I’ll just go ahead and say that this is
my new favorite Marvel movie. It hits all

00:04:27.930 --> 00:04:33.960
the right action movie beats and all of the
characters land. Visually it’s so much more

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:39.680
interesting than the other Marvel movies you’ll
be blown away. The color Red is very very

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:44.220
important. Almost everything in the movie
has this red overcast too it and James Gunn

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:48.639
said it was his reaction to the dark brooding
science fiction movies that have come out

00:04:48.639 --> 00:04:51.520
since Blade Runner.

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:57.389
He said he wanted to return science fiction
to the pulpiness of the 50s and 60s sci fi

00:04:57.389 --> 00:05:02.889
movies just to make it feel like a more fun
movie. Not that 70s and 80s sci fi weren’t

00:05:02.889 --> 00:05:09.889
fun. He just didn’t want Guardians to feel
like a depressing pessimistic story. It’s

00:05:10.040 --> 00:05:14.889
all about childlike wonder and discovery,
which you also see in Chris Pratt’s character.

00:05:14.889 --> 00:05:17.930
So if you haven’t seen the movie yet. Just
think about the color Red when you’re sitting

00:05:17.930 --> 00:05:19.520
there in the theater.

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:24.480
You could also say that the color Red is now
a metaphor for the influence of Iron Man on

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:29.350
the marvel cinematic universe in a meta way.
Like the popularity of that character and

00:05:29.350 --> 00:05:34.740
irreverent tone of the first Iron Man film
has trickled down into all other Marvel films.

00:05:34.740 --> 00:05:39.650
But to be fair, Red is Marvel’s trademark
logo color. So Red has always been important

00:05:39.650 --> 00:05:41.340
to Marvel as a brand.

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:45.360
But all in all. I gave this movie an A plus.
I think, the only A plus I’ve given to any

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:48.860
movie this year. And there were a lot of movies
I really loved.

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:55.050
But now let’s talk about specific moments
and easter eggs so careful for spoilers if

00:05:55.050 --> 00:05:59.600
you haven’t seen the movie yet. I’ll wait
just a sec...okay, everybody ready. Here we

00:05:59.600 --> 00:05:59.990
go.

00:05:59.990 --> 00:06:05.270
My biggest surprise was how quickly they went
to Thanos and the infinity stones. I still

00:06:05.270 --> 00:06:08.600
think of them as infinity gems. Even though
I just saw the movie I’m trying to remember

00:06:08.600 --> 00:06:12.350
if Benico Del Toro called them gems or stones.
I have no idea why they feel like they need

00:06:12.350 --> 00:06:15.360
to change little details like that in the
movies, whatever.

00:06:15.360 --> 00:06:19.990
That explainer scene that he gave the Guardians
was my favorite scene in the movie. Mostly

00:06:19.990 --> 00:06:21.389
because it tells you exactly where everything
is going. It very clearly states that super

00:06:21.389 --> 00:06:25.400
powerful beings were not able to contain the
power of all six gems when they were brought

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:28.880
together. Did you notice how there was no
gauntlet in that scene.

00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:32.330
So clearly the big WTF surprise of Avengers
3 will be Thanos, harnessing the power of

00:06:32.330 --> 00:06:35.930
all six gems when he brings them together.
I feel like the real fun will be the way they

00:06:35.930 --> 00:06:38.350
express the power of each gem on screen.

00:06:38.350 --> 00:06:42.580
Here’s something weird. In the movies and
in the comics, the colors of each gem are

00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:46.889
different. Like the Space Gem, the one that
teleports things, is the cube we see in the

00:06:46.889 --> 00:06:52.060
first Avengers movie. It’s blueish. But
in the classic comics the Thanos Infinity

00:06:52.060 --> 00:06:55.740
Guantlet story, the space gem is purple like
the one we see in the Guardians movie. In

00:06:55.740 --> 00:06:56.470
the guardians movie the purple gem is the
power gem.

00:06:56.470 --> 00:06:58.889
Funny side note. In the Gauntlet comics storyline.
Drax the Destroyer is the guardian of the

00:06:58.889 --> 00:07:00.229
Power gem. Just another change from page to
screen.

00:07:00.229 --> 00:07:03.160
It gets really confusing, so be careful when
thinking about which gem is in which movie.

00:07:03.160 --> 00:07:08.400
It gets even more confusing when you consider
that Loki’s staff contains the mind gem.

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:13.120
Which also looks blueish like the tesseract
space gem. I wish there were a screen cap

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:17.620
from the movie because when Del Toro explained
everything they had this really clear graphic

00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:23.199
with six different objects in it showing each
of the gems.

00:07:23.199 --> 00:07:30.199
The sequel teasers that I got most excited
about were Peter Quill’s Father, Thanos

00:07:31.600 --> 00:07:38.460
and the Collector’s hunt for the gems and
the Guardians visiting earth.

00:07:38.460 --> 00:07:42.180
Of all those things, I don’t expect the
Guardians to visit earth in the sequel. I

00:07:42.180 --> 00:07:45.729
feel like Marvel and James Gunn will keep
all Guardians’ stories in space. It will

00:07:45.729 --> 00:07:48.160
just be the go-to space franchise.

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:53.620
I think between Avengers and Guardians, they’ll
just have individual character moonlight on

00:07:53.620 --> 00:07:57.360
each other’s team. I did a video a while
back about a certain Avenger possibly being

00:07:57.360 --> 00:07:59.960
in the Guardians sequel. I’ll post a link
to that in the description.

00:07:59.960 --> 00:08:06.960
Everyone was going crazy over the post credit
scene with Howard the Duck. I feel like the

00:08:09.720 --> 00:08:15.919
only people that will get that will be people
who have seen the Howard the Duck movie. The

00:08:15.919 --> 00:08:20.009
reason it’s in Guardians because of Gene
Colan. He was the artist that originated Guardians

00:08:20.009 --> 00:08:24.389
of the Galaxy and he had a hand in originating
Howard the Duck. Howard the Duck is a Marvel

00:08:24.389 --> 00:08:24.490
character.

00:08:24.490 --> 00:08:27.910
So it’s a comic book easter egg, but you
could also consider it an easter egg for the

00:08:27.910 --> 00:08:34.380
80s movie too. That was a lucasfilm movie
by the way. As in Star Wars George Lucas.

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:38.520
Think of Howard the Duck as like the progenitor
or Rocket Raccoon in terms of wisecracking

00:08:38.520 --> 00:08:43.159
animals. Howard the Duck debuted in 1973 which
came after the original Guardians of the Galaxy

00:08:43.159 --> 00:08:49.279
team, which started in 1969. But that initial
team did not feature rocket raccoon. He debuted

00:08:49.279 --> 00:08:50.820
in 1976.

00:08:50.820 --> 00:08:57.820
The Guardians in this movie are much closer
to the Annhiliation Conquest arc. They rebooted

00:08:58.680 --> 00:09:03.710
the comic again in 2013 too. So if you’re
looking for comics to read, I’d just start

00:09:03.710 --> 00:09:07.050
with the reboot. It features Iron Man joining
the Guardians. It’s really cool, there’s

00:09:07.050 --> 00:09:11.660
a really funny sex scene between him and Gamora.

00:09:11.660 --> 00:09:16.760
Here’s some of the biggest easter eggs in
the movie:

00:09:16.760 --> 00:09:20.470
Peter Quill’s spaceship, the Milano, is
actually named after the character’s childhood

00:09:20.470 --> 00:09:26.760
crush Alyssa Milano. Remember he’s a 70s
and 80s pop culture junkie. So a lot of his

00:09:26.760 --> 00:09:31.770
references are frozen at the point where he
left the earth. In the 1980s. He probably

00:09:31.770 --> 00:09:36.339
hasn’t seen any movies, tv shows or music
from after that point. So he doesn’t know

00:09:36.339 --> 00:09:40.540
who Justin Bieber is. Imagine his disappointment
when he learns about that.

00:09:40.540 --> 00:09:45.140
How funny was it that he called Kevin Bacon
one of the greatest hero’s ever. The Legend

00:09:45.140 --> 00:09:46.339
of Footloose.

00:09:46.339 --> 00:09:52.970
Inside the collector’s museum there’s
Cosmo, A Dark Elf, a Chitauri and a slug from

00:09:52.970 --> 00:09:56.010
James Gunn’s earlier movie Slither. Starring
Nathan Fillion.

00:09:56.010 --> 00:10:00.680
Nathan Fillion’s cameo in the movie is almost
unrecognizable. He’s the giant alien who

00:10:00.680 --> 00:10:05.110
gets Groot’s branches stuck up his nose.
You can kind of tell it’s him by the voice.

00:10:05.110 --> 00:10:08.930
Stan Lee’s cameo is pretty obvious, but
it’s hilarious that Rocket calls him on

00:10:08.930 --> 00:10:10.120
being a total creeper.

00:10:10.120 --> 00:10:14.180
Rob Zombie had a voice only cameo as the navigator
of Yondu’s ship.

00:10:14.180 --> 00:10:18.529
And James Gunn’s mentor Lloyd Kaufmann was
a prison in the Kyln scenes.

00:10:18.529 --> 00:10:22.459
I guess you could consider Knowhere to be
an easter egg even though they call it out

00:10:22.459 --> 00:10:27.320
verbally. In the comics people can use the
brain stem of the ancient celestial to travel

00:10:27.320 --> 00:10:30.930
anywhere in space and time. We haven’t really
dealt with time travel in the marvel cinematic

00:10:30.930 --> 00:10:33.940
universe yet though.

00:10:33.940 --> 00:10:39.680
That opening scene is a pretty clear riff
on Raiders of The Lost Arc. If only Indy had

00:10:39.680 --> 00:10:43.110
a magnet to draw the idol off the trap.

00:10:43.110 --> 00:10:48.160
There are five big planets that the movie
features that were also part of big comic

00:10:48.160 --> 00:10:48.850
book storylines too.

00:10:48.850 --> 00:10:53.940
Hala the Kree homeworld debuted in the comics
about the same time Captain Mar-Vell, that’s

00:10:53.940 --> 00:10:56.970
Mar-Vell, not Captain Marvel, different characters.

00:10:56.970 --> 00:11:01.690
Xandar is the homebase of the Nova Corps and
Richard Ryder, the superhero Nova. James Gunn

00:11:01.690 --> 00:11:05.140
said he kind of hates that character so he
might not make it into the sequel. He says

00:11:05.140 --> 00:11:09.330
it’s the helmet. He hates the helmet. The
planet was destroyed during the Annihilation

00:11:09.330 --> 00:11:10.830
Conquest storyline.

00:11:10.830 --> 00:11:17.830
The Kyln has always been a prison. Even Thanos
was kept there for a while.

00:11:19.600 --> 00:11:24.320
Knowhere I already talked about. In the comics
Cosmo the Space Dog was actually administrator

00:11:24.320 --> 00:11:27.800
there. Clearly something James Gunn changed.

00:11:27.800 --> 00:11:31.529
Morag 4, the planet where the Orb was found
was featured during Annihilation Conquest.

00:11:31.529 --> 00:11:34.220
It featured a pretty epic battle between Quasar
and Moondragon.

00:11:34.220 --> 00:11:41.220
In terms of storylines for the sequel I think
Thanos Imperative, War of Kings and Annihilation

00:11:41.459 --> 00:11:44.290
Conquest are all good places to draw from.
Thanos Imperative was like the culmination

00:11:44.290 --> 00:11:48.050
of Conquest and War of Kings though, so they’d
have to establish Inhumans and a few other

00:11:48.050 --> 00:11:55.050
things before dealing with the Cancerverse
and a fully formed infinity gauntlet.

00:11:57.110 --> 00:12:00.839
Quick sidenote, Inhumans could totally be
one of those 6 new mystery Marvel movies.

00:12:00.839 --> 00:12:05.029
I still need to do an Inhumans video at some
point.

00:12:05.029 --> 00:12:07.820
But let me know what your favorite part of
the movie was and what story do you want to

00:12:07.820 --> 00:12:09.940
see the sequel take on?

00:12:09.940 --> 00:12:16.320
My next Marvel video will be a deeper exploration
of Guardians 2 stories. Be sure to subscribe

00:12:16.320 --> 00:12:19.240
to get it. I’ll try to post it early next
week.

